<%
  source_file = @source&.file&.attached? ? "[#{@source.file.filename}](#{rails_blob_url(@source.file)})" : "missing"
  missing = []
%>
# Post #<%= @post.id %> — <%= @preset.name %>

- Studio: <%= post_url(@post) %>
- Preset: `<%= @post.preset_slug %>`
- Transition: <%= @post.transition_label %>
- Source (v0): <%= @source ? "media bank ##{@source.id} #{source_file}" : "(none)" %>
- Rules (order): <%= @post.rules_list.join(" → ").presence || "(none)" %>

## Agent task

Fill missing key frames for this post. Full procedure: [docs/POST_FRAMES.md](/docs/POST_FRAMES.md).

1. Work **one rule at a time**, in the order below.
2. For each missing `vN`: call **GenerateImage** with the rule's **Image prompt**, `reference_image_paths` = the previous still (v0 source, else the last attached frame), aspect matching the source.
3. Attach the result as `PostFrame` position `N` / `rule_number` via `bin/rails runner` (snippet in POST_FRAMES.md).
4. Stop when every rule has an attached frame. Do not re-generate attached frames unless asked.

## Frames
<% @post.rules_list.each_with_index do |number, i| %>
<%
  position = i + 1
  rule = @rules[number]
  frame = @post.frame_at(position)
  attached = frame&.file&.attached?
  missing << "v#{position}" unless attached
  ref = i.zero? ? "v0 (source)" : "v#{i}"
%>
### v<%= position %> · rule #<%= number %><%= rule ? " — #{rule.title}" : "" %>

- Status: <%= attached ? "attached [#{frame.file.filename}](#{rails_blob_url(frame.file)})" : "**missing** — generate from #{ref}" %>
- Studio scene: <%= post_url(@post, scene: "v#{position}") %>
<% if rule&.prompt.present? %>

Image prompt:

~~~text
<%= rule.prompt %>
~~~
<% elsif rule %>

Image prompt: _(empty on GuideRule #<%= number %> — write one from the rule body before generating)_
<% else %>

Image prompt: _(no GuideRule ##<%= number %> on this preset's guide)_
<% end %>
<% end %>
<% if @post.rules_list.empty? %>

_(No rules on this post — nothing to generate.)_
<% elsif missing.empty? %>

All frames attached.
<% else %>

Still missing: <%= missing.join(", ") %>.
<% end %>
